WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.300 --> 00:00:03.580
I downloaded the NIOH demo on its last day, and...

00:00:03.820 --> 00:00:05.180
I've made a mistake.

00:00:05.420 --> 00:00:06.860
This game is amazing,

00:00:07.120 --> 00:00:09.680
and I have less than 24 hours to play it.

00:00:10.400 --> 00:00:14.380
So I opened my notepad, I start taking a few notes on the game, and...

00:00:14.440 --> 00:00:19.800
then I discard that idea because I do not intend on putting this controller down.

00:00:20.080 --> 00:00:22.460
I have this legitimate hunger for the combat.

00:00:22.460 --> 00:00:27.740
Just to dive in and kill enemies and push a little bit further than I got last time.

00:00:28.060 --> 00:00:29.900
And that's a damn good sign.

00:00:30.280 --> 00:00:34.980
So, here's what I learned, and here's what I was impressed with from my short time playing.

00:00:37.740 --> 00:00:42.080
In this game, stamina is called "Ki," and it's key that you manage your ki

00:00:42.080 --> 00:00:44.080
and the ki of your opponent.

00:00:44.500 --> 00:00:45.900
With this new information,

00:00:45.900 --> 00:00:49.660
you have to power to see how far your enemy can exert themselves,

00:00:49.900 --> 00:00:52.700
when they're about to overextend, and...

00:00:52.700 --> 00:00:56.340
when the right moment is to overwhelm them and punish them.

00:01:00.200 --> 00:01:03.520
Right off the bat, this adds a huge depth to the combat system.

00:01:03.520 --> 00:01:09.460
But most importantly, perhaps, stamina vision affords you this reassuring feeling that...

00:01:09.460 --> 00:01:14.340
The opponents you're facing are operating on the same rules that you are, as a player.

00:01:14.700 --> 00:01:17.220
The game, itself, isn't trying to kill you,

00:01:17.220 --> 00:01:19.640
the AI, within the game, are.

00:01:19.640 --> 00:01:23.940
And I think that's a humanizing rule of design that more games should follow.

00:01:23.940 --> 00:01:29.340
Especially games like this, that go even beyond Dark Souls in terms of how hard they are.

00:01:30.400 --> 00:01:35.100
An additional mechanic, to make stamina more interactive is "The Ki Pulse."

00:01:35.320 --> 00:01:39.420
If you press R1 the moment after expending your ki,

00:01:39.420 --> 00:01:44.800
then you'll perform this 'pulse,' which, immediately regenerates the ki you just expended.

00:01:44.880 --> 00:01:48.480
The amount is signified by this fast-moving blue bar.

00:01:48.900 --> 00:01:53.260
And doing this pulse properly enforces this flow upon combat,

00:01:53.500 --> 00:01:59.480
which, if followed appropriately, gives you a huge ki advantage over your opponents.

00:01:59.680 --> 00:02:00.180
And,

00:02:00.180 --> 00:02:03.160
it just allows you to attack like an absolute demon,

00:02:03.160 --> 00:02:06.020
provided you can keep up the appropriate pacing.

00:02:06.880 --> 00:02:12.700
Also, this 'pulse' can cleanse the aura given off by enemies from the Yokyra.

00:02:13.100 --> 00:02:15.720
It's this black fog that, if you step in it,

00:02:16.040 --> 00:02:18.300
stops you regenerating your ki.

00:02:18.700 --> 00:02:21.480
So, performing the pulse to cleanse this

00:02:21.540 --> 00:02:25.280
felt, to me, like a forceful way of teaching me that

00:02:25.480 --> 00:02:29.200
the ki pulse habit is probably one I should get into.

00:02:29.200 --> 00:02:35.260
Unfortunately I didn't during my time in the demo and I have a huge feeling that made the game much, much harder for myself,

00:02:35.540 --> 00:02:37.680
because I didn't start doing this.

00:02:38.220 --> 00:02:43.420
But, anyway, all of this makes NIOH the first souls-like game that I've played

00:02:43.660 --> 00:02:47.480
that puts stamina at the very core of the game, where

00:02:47.480 --> 00:02:49.400
it rightfully belongs.

00:02:49.720 --> 00:02:52.860
This fits into this combat system that rewards awareness.

00:02:52.860 --> 00:02:58.620
And it's not just awareness of stamina, it's also awareness of the attacks of enemies of course.

00:02:58.640 --> 00:03:02.240
And in these kinds of games, enemy attacks should have

00:03:02.360 --> 00:03:05.480
two parts. There's the forecast of the attack.

00:03:05.480 --> 00:03:07.700
And then there's the attack itself.

00:03:08.000 --> 00:03:10.840
There's this raising, or lowering, of the weapon.

00:03:10.940 --> 00:03:11.980
Then the swing,

00:03:12.200 --> 00:03:14.960
allowing you to predict and react.

00:03:15.160 --> 00:03:18.080
The animation is fantastic. For the most part.

00:03:18.460 --> 00:03:21.320
Except on some of the larger monsters.

00:03:21.320 --> 00:03:26.020
For example, this one boss had this spin attack that I never really felt like I deserved

00:03:26.020 --> 00:03:27.040
getting hit by.

00:03:27.040 --> 00:03:29.140
And, they need to be careful to get this right.

00:03:29.140 --> 00:03:32.500
Because I think it's the most important thing about the combat.

00:03:33.180 --> 00:03:35.580
One thing that took a lot of getting used to, is

00:03:35.580 --> 00:03:40.360
the sheer variety of movesets that are available to both you and your opponents.

00:03:40.960 --> 00:03:47.460
In NIOH, there is a selection of weapon classes like spear, hammer, katana, and dual-katana,

00:03:47.760 --> 00:03:52.800
and while every weapon within that class appears to share the same moveset,

00:03:53.120 --> 00:03:57.480
every class of weapon can be held in one of three stances.

00:03:57.900 --> 00:04:01.580
So high stance gives you powerful, but slower attacks.

00:04:01.920 --> 00:04:04.960
Low stance gives you fast, but weaker attacks, and

00:04:05.380 --> 00:04:08.800
Mid stance is, predictably, the balance between the two.

00:04:09.100 --> 00:04:12.880
And in each stance, you still have access to light and heavy attacks,

00:04:12.880 --> 00:04:16.300
and these attacks are different depending on what stance you're in.

00:04:16.700 --> 00:04:17.200
So,

00:04:17.440 --> 00:04:20.300
basically you can swap attack style on the fly,

00:04:20.300 --> 00:04:21.800
and that feels fanastic.

00:04:21.800 --> 00:04:24.500
It's quite like Bloodborne, in that regard.

00:04:24.500 --> 00:04:29.900
Just, instead of having two weapons states, every weapon has three weapon states, and

00:04:30.040 --> 00:04:36.180
it means you can proactively adapt to combat in a way that you never really do in Souls games

00:04:36.180 --> 00:04:41.520
Giving you access to thrust attacks, overhead attacks, fast attacks, slow attacks...

00:04:41.780 --> 00:04:44.660
All regardless of the weapon you're using.

00:04:44.980 --> 00:04:49.320
And, you might already be thinking about this, that the obvious risk here is that

00:04:49.320 --> 00:04:54.580
because you can cover the weakness of every single weapon by changing stances,

00:04:54.900 --> 00:04:57.960
that weapons might struggle to feel unique.

00:04:57.960 --> 00:05:03.780
Because what's the point in using a great-hammer if I can just put it in a light stance to attack quickly, or

00:05:03.780 --> 00:05:08.640
what's the point of using dual-katanas if I can put it in a slow stance to make them

00:05:08.820 --> 00:05:09.860
more powerful?

00:05:10.040 --> 00:05:10.540
So,

00:05:10.600 --> 00:05:11.100
yeah.

00:05:11.200 --> 00:05:14.880
This does affect the individuality of weapon classes.

00:05:15.300 --> 00:05:17.660
And, sure, you could argue that,

00:05:17.660 --> 00:05:23.800
yes, the low stance of the dual-katanas is still faster than the low stance of the great hammer.

00:05:23.900 --> 00:05:24.400
But,

00:05:24.400 --> 00:05:30.760
there's so much coverage here, and this approach does mean that weapons lose some individuality.

00:05:31.180 --> 00:05:32.780
But do I want it changed?

00:05:32.920 --> 00:05:33.420
Nope.

00:05:33.800 --> 00:05:37.880
Like I said, it feels fantastic to have complete control of your weapon.

00:05:37.880 --> 00:05:41.740
And the only thing holding you back in combat is really your awareness, and

00:05:41.740 --> 00:05:45.500
your knowledge of how well your stance will fit the situation.

00:05:45.500 --> 00:05:50.160
I think that build diversity is going to struggle a bit in the long-run because of this,

00:05:50.480 --> 00:05:54.760
but there is so much depth to the combat that I don't see this being a big issue.

00:05:55.080 --> 00:06:00.320
And, for all the individuality weapons lose from stances, they do gain some character back

00:06:00.320 --> 00:06:03.760
with the option to learn weapon-specific abilities.

00:06:04.280 --> 00:06:07.400
You can invest 'talent points' into new abilities,

00:06:07.400 --> 00:06:13.000
which are specific to each weapon class, like the powerful spin attack of the great hammer,

00:06:13.180 --> 00:06:15.580
or the wily trip attack of the spear.

00:06:16.260 --> 00:06:22.240
And also, you can find the same type of weapon with different rarities and attributes,

00:06:22.240 --> 00:06:25.640
and that helps make your weapon feel a bit more unique.

00:06:26.360 --> 00:06:28.540
I'd also like to praise the level design.

00:06:28.540 --> 00:06:34.860
Particularly for the way that these felt like real coast-lines, real villages, real forests, and

00:06:34.860 --> 00:06:37.900
I liked the way they blended environments together, and

00:06:37.920 --> 00:06:41.600
all the while, they were hiding a bunch of estus shards,

00:06:41.760 --> 00:06:45.620
physical shortcuts, and, most notably, ambushes.

00:06:45.840 --> 00:06:48.800
Because of these, I was progressing slowly.

00:06:48.800 --> 00:06:54.000
Peaking around corners and just listening for that audio cue that signals you're in trouble.

00:06:54.440 --> 00:06:57.080
There was no real cue for this happening, however.

00:07:00.080 --> 00:07:05.400
And speaking of falling, I like how knocking enemies off edges is actually encouraged by the level design,

00:07:05.460 --> 00:07:06.500
and the combat.

00:07:06.500 --> 00:07:12.300
Because if you strike an enemy towards the edge, then they'll clip into this falling animation that's...

00:07:12.300 --> 00:07:14.420
Incredibly satisfying to pull off.

00:07:14.740 --> 00:07:19.300
And, this ability to jostle for space, and knock enemies off ledges,

00:07:19.300 --> 00:07:22.340
it's supported by the combat much more than in Souls.

00:07:22.400 --> 00:07:26.320
Because if you hit an enemy in this game, or if you take a hit,

00:07:26.320 --> 00:07:32.180
there is a lot more backstep and movement during attacks that you need to take into account.

00:07:32.900 --> 00:07:36.420
Now, it is possible to comfortably run past enemies,

00:07:36.420 --> 00:07:39.940
but this demo had a lot of decent choke-points.

00:07:39.940 --> 00:07:42.520
That's something that Dark Souls never does well,

00:07:42.520 --> 00:07:47.880
you can always sprint past stuff and then initiate the  invincibility frames when you're opening a door.

00:07:47.880 --> 00:07:48.900
But, no,

00:07:48.900 --> 00:07:51.980
in this game, if you're climbing a ladder and you get hit once,

00:07:51.980 --> 00:07:57.900
you fall off, and good luck killing a mini-boss that's a required kill when you're followed by

00:07:57.900 --> 00:08:02.420
all the enemies that you've accrued from running for five minutes straight.

00:08:02.560 --> 00:08:06.880
I was always punished for fighting in unfamiliar territory, and

00:08:06.880 --> 00:08:08.060
that's a good thing.

00:08:08.500 --> 00:08:12.160
You're also rewarded for fighting some enemies, as

00:08:12.160 --> 00:08:16.340
the Yokai monsters don't respawn if you kill them once.

00:08:16.720 --> 00:08:20.360
Which allows them to server as a sort of soft checkpoint system.

00:08:20.780 --> 00:08:26.140
And, I probably shouldn't talk about the game too much longer, because I didn't get enough time with NIOH

00:08:26.180 --> 00:08:28.040
to talk confidently about it

00:08:28.520 --> 00:08:29.020
But,

00:08:29.460 --> 00:08:33.440
man, considering how much fun I had with it, and how hyped I am for it now...

00:08:33.440 --> 00:08:35.640
I just couldn't resist making a video.

00:08:35.640 --> 00:08:40.820
But, rest assured that when this game does come out on February 19th, 2017,

00:08:41.080 --> 00:08:44.140
I will try to make the best damn NIOH video you've ever seen,

00:08:44.460 --> 00:08:47.880
but for now, I'm going to direct you over to three channels,

00:08:47.880 --> 00:08:49.660
There's TerraMantis's channel,

00:08:49.680 --> 00:08:52.560
he has a great video on NIOH's multiplayer.

00:08:52.820 --> 00:08:55.920
And, I'm going to direct you to a smaller channel I found,

00:08:55.920 --> 00:09:00.420
called HustleHabit for a chilled out discussion about the depth in the game.

00:09:00.540 --> 00:09:04.700
And, also Silver Mont has this fantastic video talking about

00:09:05.040 --> 00:09:08.980
how well the developer listened to feedback since their previous demo.

00:09:08.980 --> 00:09:12.100
Which, you really do have to give the dev props for.

00:09:12.340 --> 00:09:14.280
From his video I got the impression

00:09:14.280 --> 00:09:17.640
that they literally took his advice on some topics,

00:09:18.000 --> 00:09:21.940
they've even reached out to me to hear what scant feedback I have,

00:09:21.940 --> 00:09:24.000
and that's super humbling, and

00:09:24.000 --> 00:09:25.080
very promising.

00:09:25.800 --> 00:09:28.460
We've covered a few souls-like games at this point...

00:09:28.700 --> 00:09:31.260
Some of them take the Souls formula and

00:09:31.620 --> 00:09:35.500
they apply it cleverly to an entirely different 2D perspective.

00:09:35.900 --> 00:09:40.680
Some take a few elements or twist them and they build them up, and

00:09:40.680 --> 00:09:43.080
turn the game into something else...

00:09:43.080 --> 00:09:45.200
And sometimes something better.

00:09:45.200 --> 00:09:49.340
These little risks can show how the formula of Souls can be improved

00:09:49.360 --> 00:09:53.280
and they're the way these games can continue to feel fresh.

00:09:53.360 --> 00:09:58.160
And I'm expecting a lot of great things from NIOH when I pick it up for PS4.

00:09:58.560 --> 00:10:00.260
So, thanks for watching guys, and

00:10:00.260 --> 00:10:01.540
I'll see you in the next one.

